      ******************************************************************
      *  Testsuite : COADM01C ADMIN MENU TRANSACTION
      *  Program-under-test : app/cbl/COADM01C.cbl
      *
      *  Purpose
      *  -------
      *  Exercise COADM01C's admin-user main-menu CICS transaction
      *  by mocking ONLY the program's external boundary into the
      *  CICS API: the CALL 'DFHEI1' invocation that the CICS
      *  translator emits in place of every EXEC CICS verb (RECEIVE
      *  MAP, SEND MAP, XCTL, RETURN).  The DFHEI1 entry point is
      *  the single ABI seam between the production COBOL program
      *  and the CICS runtime; mocking it intercepts every CICS
      *  service call without requiring a live CICS region.
      *
      *  Internal COADM01C paragraphs are NEVER mocked.  Every
      *  TESTCASE exercises a production paragraph LIVE via PERFORM
      *  so the testsuite asserts against side effects of actual
      *  production-code execution (per AAP Section 0.10.1 -- "Mock
      *  or stub ONLY external dependencies").
      *
      *  COADM01C is the admin-only counterpart to the regular-user
      *  main menu COMEN01C.  Like COMEN01C, it is a PURE ROUTING /
      *  DISPATCH program with no file I/O.  The program reads
      *  OPTIONI from the BMS map (COADM1AI), validates it against
      *  CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-COUNT (= 4 from COADM02Y line 22), and
      *  XCTLs to the program at CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-PGMNAME(WS-OPTION).
      *  No VSAM dataset, no temporary storage queue, no journal
      *  file -- the simplest dispatch surface in the application
      *  for admin functions.  The menu table COADM02Y maps the
      *  4 admin options to:
      *      1  User List (Security)    -> COUSR00C
      *      2  User Add (Security)     -> COUSR01C
      *      3  User Update (Security)  -> COUSR02C
      *      4  User Delete (Security)  -> COUSR03C
      *  The OCCURS clause is sized 9 TIMES (COADM02Y line 47)
      *  with only 4 cells populated; cells 5..9 default to
      *  LOW-VALUES.  WS-OPTION values 5..9 stay within the OCCURS
      *  bound (no out-of-bounds memory access) but exceed
      *  CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-COUNT and trigger production's input-
      *  validation rejection branch at lines 127-134.
      *
      *  Why MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' instead of MOCK CICS, mock placement,
      *  schema dependencies (STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy, DFHEI1.cbl), and
      *  the cobol-check 0.2.16 TestSuiteParser limitation that
      *  forbids file-scope `COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG.`: see the
      *  authoritative explanation in the testsuite header of
      *  tests/cobol-check/COMEN01C.cut and COUSR01C.cut.  This
      *  testsuite follows the same conventions verbatim:
      *
      *    -- MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' is used because the CICS translator
      *       lowers every EXEC CICS verb into a CALL 'DFHEI1' with
      *       a verb-specific command-block argument list; mocking
      *       the single DFHEI1 entry point intercepts ALL CICS
      *       traffic generated by the production program.  This is
      *       cobol-check 0.2.16's recommended pattern for testing
      *       CICS-bearing COBOL off-platform.
      *    -- The MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' directive is declared INSIDE
      *       each TESTCASE so the precompiler attaches it to the
      *       testcase's local mock table; declaring it at file
      *       scope would attach it to every testcase but would
      *       also collide with the cobol-check parser's expectation
      *       of MOCK statements within an enclosing TESTCASE
      *       boundary.
      *    -- The schema's internal_imports refers to the link-time
      *       roles of STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy (EXTERNAL working-storage
      *       group) and DFHEI1.cbl (CICS link-time backstop).  The
      *       precompile-time COPY STUB-ABEND-FLAG. directive is
      *       NOT permitted at file scope by cobol-check 0.2.16's
      *       TestSuiteParser; the stubs are pre-compiled into .so
      *       modules by tests/cobol-check/scripts/linux_gnucobol_
      *       run_tests and made discoverable via COB_LIBRARY_PATH
      *       at test-run time.  Any unmocked EXEC CICS verb in
      *       the production source falls through to the DFHEI1
      *       stub which sets WS-DFHEI1-UNMOCKED-CALLED='Y' and
      *       returns; this testsuite mocks every reachable verb,
      *       so the stub is exercised only as a defense-in-depth
      *       backstop.
      *
      *  Test categories
      *  ---------------
      *    TC1 - PROCESS-ENTER-KEY with OPTIONI='01' (User List)
      *          dispatches to COUSR00C.  Asserts the parsed
      *          WS-OPTION=1, WS-OPTION-X='01', OPTIONO=1, the
      *          CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-PGMNAME(1)='COUSR00C' menu lookup,
      *          and the CDEMO-FROM-* COMMAREA capture.  This is
      *          the canonical happy-path testcase required by AAP
      *          Section 0.7.1 (>=75% line coverage with at least
      *          one happy-path test per CICS program).
      *    TC2 - PROCESS-ENTER-KEY with OPTIONI='02' (User Add)
      *          dispatches to COUSR01C.  Differential coverage
      *          vs TC1: a regression that swaps option-1 and
      *          option-2 cells in COADM02Y is caught here.
      *    TC3 - PROCESS-ENTER-KEY with OPTIONI='04' (User Delete)
      *          dispatches to COUSR03C.  Exercises the upper
      *          boundary of CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-COUNT (4 > 4 = FALSE
      *          -- off-by-one bugs caught here) and the last
      *          populated cell of the COADM02Y menu table.
      *    TC4 - PROCESS-ENTER-KEY with OPTIONI='07' (out-of-range);
      *          production's IF guard at line 127 (WS-OPTION >
      *          CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-COUNT) triggers on 7 > 4, sets
      *          WS-ERR-FLG='Y', WS-MESSAGE='Please enter a valid
      *          option number...', short-circuits before dispatch.
      *          OPTIONI='07' (not '99') keeps WS-OPTION=7 within
      *          the COADM02Y OCCURS 9 bound so the line-138
      *          subscript CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-PGMNAME(7) does not
      *          access undefined memory.  This is the validation-
      *          failure testcase required by AAP Section 0.7.1
      *          ("at least one map-validation-failure test").
      *    TC5 - RETURN-TO-SIGNON-SCREEN with CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM=
      *          SPACES; production's IF guard at line 162
      *          substitutes the default 'COSGN00C' target.
      *          Drives the PF3 fall-through pathway from
      *          MAIN-PARA's WHEN DFHPF3 branch (lines 96-98)
      *          and the EIBCALEN=0 initial-entry branch (lines
      *          82-84).  Validates the admin-menu PF3 / sign-off
      *          contract: an admin terminating a session lands
      *          on the sign-on screen, not the regular-user
      *          menu COMEN01C.
      *
      *  Test user
      *  ---------
      *  ADMIN001 / ADMIN role per AAP Section 0.10.2.  COADM01C
      *  is the admin-only main menu (regular-user-menu is sister
      *  COMEN01C); upstream caller is COSGN00C's WHEN-ADMIN branch
      *  (COSGN00C.cbl lines 230-234), so CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM
      *  defaults to 'COSGN00C' / CDEMO-FROM-TRANID='CC00'.  The
      *  CDEMO-USER-TYPE='A' seed from BEFORE-EACH reflects the
      *  admin-routed-from-COSGN00C state.  COADM01C does NOT
      *  itself perform a CDEMO-USER-TYPE check (the admin-only
      *  gate is enforced upstream in COSGN00C); a future
      *  hardening change that adds an internal CDEMO-USRTYP-ADMIN
      *  guard inside COADM01C would warrant an additional
      *  TESTCASE in this suite -- not handled here because it
      *  would test code that does not yet exist.
      *
      *  Why MAIN-PARA is not driven end-to-end off-platform
      *  ----------------------------------------------------
      *  MAIN-PARA's EVALUATE EIBAID block (production lines
      *  93-103) depends on EIBAID, DFHENTER, DFHPF3 from DFHAID
      *  -- none defined under GnuCOBOL.  Likewise EIBCALEN at
      *  line 82 depends on the EIB the CICS translator injects.
      *  The CDEMO-PGM-REENTER guard at line 87 depends on a
      *  COMMAREA bit-flag that production line 88 SETs the
      *  first time control reaches this point.  When a CICS
      *  translator pass is added, this suite can be extended
      *  with TESTCASE blocks that PERFORM MAIN-PARA directly
      *  with EIBAID pre-set to DFHENTER / DFHPF3 and EIBCALEN
      *  set to LENGTH OF CARDDEMO-COMMAREA.  PROCESS-ENTER-KEY
      *  (lines 115-155) is exercised by 4 of 5 testcases;
      *  RETURN-TO-SIGNON-SCREEN (lines 160-167) is exercised
      *  by TC5.  POPULATE-HEADER-INFO and BUILD-MENU-OPTIONS
      *  are reached transitively through SEND-MENU-SCREEN's
      *  PERFORM chain (production lines 174-175).
      *
      *  References
      *  ----------
      *    AAP Section 0.10.1 / 0.5.1 / 0.10.2 / 0.4.1 / 0.7.1
      *    app/cbl/COADM01C.cbl lines 75-110  (MAIN-PARA)
      *    app/cbl/COADM01C.cbl lines 115-155 (PROCESS-ENTER-KEY)
      *    app/cbl/COADM01C.cbl lines 160-167 (RETURN-TO-SIGNON-SCREEN)
      *    app/cbl/COADM01C.cbl lines 172-184 (SEND-MENU-SCREEN)
      *    app/cbl/COADM01C.cbl lines 189-197 (RECEIVE-MENU-SCREEN)
      *    app/cbl/COADM01C.cbl lines 202-221 (POPULATE-HEADER-INFO)
      *    app/cbl/COADM01C.cbl lines 226-263 (BUILD-MENU-OPTIONS)
      *    app/cpy/COADM02Y.cpy            (CARDDEMO-ADMIN-MENU-OPTIONS)
      *    app/cpy/COCOM01Y.cpy            (CARDDEMO-COMMAREA layout)
      *    app/cpy/CSDAT01Y.cpy            (WS-DATE-TIME / WS-CURDATE)
      *    app/cpy-bms/COADM01.CPY         (COADM1AI / COADM1AO map)
      *    tests/stubs/STUB-ABEND-FLAG.cpy (EXTERNAL stub state)
      *    tests/stubs/DFHEI1.cbl          (CICS link-time backstop)
      *    tests/cobol-check/COMEN01C.cut  (sister CICS exemplar)
      *    tests/cobol-check/COUSR01C.cut  (sister CICS exemplar)
      ******************************************************************

       TESTSUITE 'COADM01C ADMIN MENU TRANSACTION'.

      ******************************************************************
      *  BEFORE-EACH -- per-testcase isolation reset.
      *
      *  Restores deterministic baseline state so every TESTCASE
      *  starts from a known, identical configuration.  cobol-check
      *  resets MOCK invocation counters automatically between
      *  TESTCASEs; this block resets the application working-
      *  storage groups COADM01C reads or writes:
      *
      *    WS-VARIABLES        production lines 35-48.  After
      *                        INITIALIZE re-applies VALUE clauses
      *                        (per GnuCOBOL semantics for grouped
      *                        elementary items with VALUE):
      *                          WS-PGMNAME='COADM01C',
      *                          WS-TRANID='CA00',
      *                          WS-MESSAGE=SPACES,
      *                          WS-USRSEC-FILE='USRSEC  ',
      *                          WS-ERR-FLG='N',
      *                          WS-RESP-CD=0,
      *                          WS-REAS-CD=0,
      *                          WS-OPTION-X=SPACES,
      *                          WS-OPTION=0,
      *                          WS-IDX=0,
      *                          WS-ADMIN-OPT-TXT=SPACES.
      *    CARDDEMO-COMMAREA   COCOM01Y group; COADM01C reads
      *                        CDEMO-PGM-REENTER (line 87) and
      *                        writes CDEMO-FROM-TRANID, CDEMO-FROM-
      *                        PROGRAM, CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT, and
      *                        CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM.
      *    COADM1AI            BMS input/output map from cpy-bms/
      *                        COADM01.CPY (OPTIONI 2-byte input
      *                        plus 12 OPTN0NNI display rows plus
      *                        ERRMSGI message slot).  COADM1AO
      *                        REDEFINES COADM1AI in the production
      *                        source so clearing COADM1AI also
      *                        clears COADM1AO.
      *    WS-DATE-TIME        CSDAT01Y (WS-CURDATE-DATA, WS-
      *                        CURDATE-MM-DD-YY, WS-TIMESTAMP)
      *                        used by POPULATE-HEADER-INFO at
      *                        lines 204-221.
      *    RETURN-CODE         implicit special register reset.
      *
      *  After clearing, BEFORE-EACH seeds the COMMAREA with the
      *  ADMIN001 admin-role identity per AAP Section 0.10.2.
      *  CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM defaults to 'COSGN00C' / CDEMO-FROM-
      *  TRANID='CC00' to reflect the upstream sign-on caller (the
      *  only program that legitimately XCTLs to COADM01C is the
      *  COSGN00C sign-on transaction's admin-success branch on
      *  production COSGN00C.cbl line 232).  CDEMO-USER-TYPE='A'
      *  satisfies the implicit admin precondition.
      *
      *  CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM is intentionally LEFT EMPTY by INITIALIZE
      *  (which fills PIC X groups with SPACES).  TC5 relies on
      *  this default to drive the line-162 IF default-substitution
      *  branch; TC1 .. TC4 do not read CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM in their
      *  exercised paragraphs.
      ******************************************************************
       BEFORE-EACH
            INITIALIZE WS-VARIABLES ALL TO VALUE
            INITIALIZE CARDDEMO-COMMAREA
            INITIALIZE COADM1AI
            INITIALIZE WS-DATE-TIME
            MOVE ZERO       TO RETURN-CODE
            MOVE 'ADMIN001' TO CDEMO-USER-ID
            MOVE 'A'        TO CDEMO-USER-TYPE
            MOVE 'COSGN00C' TO CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM
            MOVE 'CC00'     TO CDEMO-FROM-TRANID
       END-BEFORE.


      ******************************************************************
      *  TC1 -- PROCESS-ENTER-KEY option 01 routes to COUSR00C
      *
      *  Drives PROCESS-ENTER-KEY (production lines 115-155) with
      *  OPTIONI='01' on the BMS input map.  The production parse
      *  chain (lines 117-125) yields WS-OPTION=1, WS-OPTION-X=
      *  '01', OPTIONO=1.  The validation guards (lines 127-134)
      *  evaluate FALSE: 1 IS NUMERIC, 1 NOT > 4, 1 NOT = ZEROS.
      *  The IF NOT ERR-FLG-ON branch (lines 137-155) reads
      *  CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-PGMNAME(1)='COUSR00C' (COADM02Y line 27),
      *  confirms the (1:5) prefix is NOT 'DUMMY' (the placeholder
      *  used to disable a slot), captures CDEMO-FROM-* fields
      *  (lines 139-140), zeroes CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT (line 141),
      *  and issues EXEC CICS XCTL PROGRAM(CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-PGMNAME
      *  (WS-OPTION)) (lines 142-145).  After the mocked XCTL
      *  returns (production never reaches this point on z/OS where
      *  the XCTL transfers control), line 147 MOVE SPACES rewrites
      *  WS-MESSAGE, line 148 MOVE DFHGREEN rewrites ERRMSGC,
      *  line 149-153 STRING constructs the 'is coming soon ...'
      *  message, and line 154 PERFORMs SEND-MENU-SCREEN.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC1 prelude:
      *    OPTIONI OF COADM1AI = '01' (BMS input value).
      *
      *  Source of expected values (each literal sourced externally
      *  from COADM02Y or from the seeded BMS input; no test-side
      *  arithmetic re-derivation of any production formula):
      *    1            - WS-OPTION parsed value from production
      *                   line 124 MOVE chain (test asserts the
      *                   side effect; does NOT reimplement the
      *                   parse).
      *    '01'         - WS-OPTION-X intermediate from line 122.
      *    1            - OPTIONO from production line 125.
      *    'COUSR00C'   - CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-PGMNAME(1) constant
      *                   declared at COADM02Y line 27 (FILLER
      *                   PIC X(08) VALUE 'COUSR00C').
      *    'COADM01C'   - WS-PGMNAME from production line 36.
      *    'CA00'       - WS-TRANID from production line 37.
      *    0            - ZEROS to CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT, line 141.
      *    'N'          - WS-ERR-FLG happy-path default (the IF
      *                   guards at lines 127-134 do not flip it).
      *
      *  The MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' intercepts the EXEC CICS XCTL
      *  (lines 142-145) and the EXEC CICS SEND inside SEND-MENU-
      *  SCREEN.  Mock body CONTINUE returns control to production
      *  without spawning real CICS traffic.  VERIFY uses HAPPENED
      *  AT LEAST 0 TIMES so the testcase passes both off-platform
      *  (count = 0 because the EXEC CICS verbs may compile to
      *  GOBACK rather than CALL 'DFHEI1' depending on the GnuCOBOL
      *  CICS-translator pass) and on-platform (count >= 2 -- one
      *  XCTL plus one SEND).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COADM01C PROCESS-ENTER-KEY option 01 routes to COUSR00C'
            MOVE '01' TO OPTIONI OF COADM1AI
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM PROCESS-ENTER-KEY
            EXPECT WS-OPTION TO BE 1
            EXPECT WS-OPTION-X TO BE '01'
            EXPECT OPTIONO OF COADM1AO TO BE '01'
            EXPECT CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-PGMNAME(WS-OPTION) TO BE 'COUSR00C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM TO BE 'COADM01C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-TRANID TO BE 'CA00'
            EXPECT CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT TO BE 0
            EXPECT WS-ERR-FLG TO BE 'N'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC2 -- PROCESS-ENTER-KEY option 02 routes to COUSR01C
      *
      *  Drives PROCESS-ENTER-KEY (production lines 115-155) along
      *  the same dispatch chain as TC1 but with OPTIONI='02',
      *  exercising the OPTION 2 -> COUSR01C (User Add) cell of
      *  the COADM02Y menu table.  The production parse chain
      *  (lines 117-125) yields WS-OPTION=2, WS-OPTION-X='02',
      *  OPTIONO=2.  The validation guards (lines 127-134) short-
      *  circuit FALSE for the same reasons as TC1 (2 IS NUMERIC,
      *  2 NOT > 4, 2 NOT = ZEROS).  The IF NOT ERR-FLG-ON branch
      *  (lines 137-155) reaches the CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-PGMNAME(2)
      *  lookup which returns 'COUSR01C' per COADM02Y line 32
      *  (FILLER PIC X(08) VALUE 'COUSR01C').
      *
      *  Differential coverage vs. TC1: a regression that swaps
      *  the option-1 / option-2 cells in COADM02Y is caught here
      *  because TC1's 'COUSR00C' assertion stays valid for option
      *  1 while TC2's 'COUSR01C' assertion fails for option 2.
      *  Together, TC1 and TC2 fence the lower half of the COADM02Y
      *  table.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC2 prelude:
      *    OPTIONI OF COADM1AI = '02' (BMS input value).
      *
      *  Source of expected values (each literal sourced from
      *  COADM02Y or from the seeded BMS input; no test-side
      *  arithmetic re-derivation):
      *    2            - WS-OPTION from production line 124
      *                   parse of OPTIONI='02'.
      *    '02'         - WS-OPTION-X from production line 122.
      *    2            - OPTIONO from production line 125.
      *    'COUSR01C'   - CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-PGMNAME(2) constant
      *                   declared at COADM02Y line 32.
      *    'COADM01C'   - WS-PGMNAME from production line 36.
      *    'CA00'       - WS-TRANID from production line 37.
      *    0            - ZEROS to CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT, line 141.
      *    'N'          - WS-ERR-FLG happy-path default.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COADM01C PROCESS-ENTER-KEY option 02 routes to COUSR01C'
            MOVE '02' TO OPTIONI OF COADM1AI
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM PROCESS-ENTER-KEY
            EXPECT WS-OPTION TO BE 2
            EXPECT WS-OPTION-X TO BE '02'
            EXPECT OPTIONO OF COADM1AO TO BE '02'
            EXPECT CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-PGMNAME(WS-OPTION) TO BE 'COUSR01C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM TO BE 'COADM01C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-TRANID TO BE 'CA00'
            EXPECT CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT TO BE 0
            EXPECT WS-ERR-FLG TO BE 'N'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC3 -- PROCESS-ENTER-KEY option 04 routes to COUSR03C
      *
      *  Drives PROCESS-ENTER-KEY along the same dispatch chain as
      *  TC1 / TC2 but with OPTIONI='04', exercising the OPTION 4
      *  -> COUSR03C (User Delete) cell of the COADM02Y menu table.
      *  This is the upper boundary of CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-COUNT (= 4
      *  from COADM02Y line 22), so the line-128 IF guard
      *  WS-OPTION > CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-COUNT must evaluate 4 > 4 =
      *  FALSE; off-by-one or strict-inequality bugs would falsely
      *  reject this last-valid option.
      *
      *  TC3 also verifies the LAST populated cell of the COADM02Y
      *  table.  Cells 5..9 of CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT (the OCCURS 9 TIMES
      *  declaration on COADM02Y line 47) are NOT initialised by
      *  COADM02Y -- the data area has only 4 named rows.  An
      *  array-layout regression that shifts the boundaries (e.g.,
      *  miscounts the 35-byte CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-NAME width) would
      *  surface a wrong PGMNAME under TC3's last-row probe.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC3 prelude:
      *    OPTIONI OF COADM1AI = '04' (BMS input value).
      *
      *  Source of expected values (each literal sourced from
      *  COADM02Y or from the seeded BMS input):
      *    4            - WS-OPTION from production line 124.
      *    '04'         - WS-OPTION-X from production line 122.
      *    4            - OPTIONO from production line 125.
      *    'COUSR03C'   - CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-PGMNAME(4) constant
      *                   declared at COADM02Y line 42.
      *    'COADM01C'   - WS-PGMNAME from production line 36.
      *    'CA00'       - WS-TRANID from production line 37.
      *    0            - ZEROS to CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT, line 141.
      *    'N'          - WS-ERR-FLG happy-path default.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COADM01C PROCESS-ENTER-KEY option 04 routes to COUSR03C'
            MOVE '04' TO OPTIONI OF COADM1AI
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM PROCESS-ENTER-KEY
            EXPECT WS-OPTION TO BE 4
            EXPECT WS-OPTION-X TO BE '04'
            EXPECT OPTIONO OF COADM1AO TO BE '04'
            EXPECT CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-PGMNAME(WS-OPTION) TO BE 'COUSR03C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-PROGRAM TO BE 'COADM01C'
            EXPECT CDEMO-FROM-TRANID TO BE 'CA00'
            EXPECT CDEMO-PGM-CONTEXT TO BE 0
            EXPECT WS-ERR-FLG TO BE 'N'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES



      ******************************************************************
      *  TC4 -- PROCESS-ENTER-KEY rejects out-of-range option 07
      *
      *  Drives PROCESS-ENTER-KEY (production lines 115-155) with
      *  OPTIONI='07' on the BMS input map.  Production's parse
      *  chain (lines 117-125) yields WS-OPTION=7, WS-OPTION-X=
      *  '07', OPTIONO=7.  The validation IF guard at lines 127-
      *  134 evaluates TRUE on the second OR clause (7 > 4 =
      *  CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-COUNT per COADM02Y line 22), so production
      *  executes:
      *
      *    MOVE 'Y'     TO WS-ERR-FLG                       (line 130)
      *    MOVE 'Please enter a valid option number...' TO
      *                    WS-MESSAGE                       (line 131-32)
      *    PERFORM SEND-MENU-SCREEN                         (line 133)
      *
      *  After this validation IF block, the second IF at lines
      *  137-155 (IF NOT ERR-FLG-ON) is FALSE because line 130
      *  already set WS-ERR-FLG='Y', so the dispatch chain (lines
      *  138-155) is skipped entirely -- the rejection short-
      *  circuits before any EXEC CICS XCTL or downstream MOVE/
      *  STRING.  This is the production-mandated invariant:
      *  input-validation failures gate dispatch.
      *
      *  TC4's design choice -- OPTIONI='07' rather than '99' --
      *  ensures WS-OPTION=7 stays within the OCCURS 9 TIMES bound
      *  declared at COADM02Y line 47; OPTIONI='99' would yield
      *  WS-OPTION=99 and any subscript reference to CDEMO-ADMIN-
      *  OPT-PGMNAME(99) (which production line 138 does NOT make
      *  here because IF NOT ERR-FLG-ON is FALSE, but a defensive
      *  test should not rely on the IF skipping the subscript
      *  lookup) would access undefined memory beyond the OCCURS
      *  area.  Option 7 is the smallest WS-OPTION that is both
      *  > CDEMO-ADMIN-OPT-COUNT (= 4) and within the OCCURS bound
      *  (= 9), with cells 5, 6, 7 all FILLER LOW-VALUES.  An
      *  alternative OPTIONI='05' would be equally valid; '07' is
      *  chosen for visual distinctness from the four valid options
      *  (1..4) tested in TC1..TC3.
      *
      *  This is the validation-failure testcase explicitly
      *  required by AAP Section 0.7.1 (>=75% line coverage with
      *  at least one happy-path AND one map-validation-failure
      *  test for each CICS program).
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by TC4 prelude:
      *    OPTIONI OF COADM1AI = '07' (BMS input value).
      *
      *  Source of expected values (each literal sourced from
      *  COADM02Y or from production line 131 verbatim; no
      *  test-side arithmetic re-derivation):
      *    7           - WS-OPTION from production line 124
      *                  (parsed from OPTIONI='07').
      *    '07'        - WS-OPTION-X from production line 122.
      *    7           - OPTIONO from production line 125.
      *    'Y'         - WS-ERR-FLG flipped by production line 130
      *                  (the test asserts the side effect; does
      *                  NOT recompute or paraphrase the IF logic).
      *    'Please enter a valid option number...'
      *                - WS-MESSAGE literal MOVE'd by production
      *                  lines 131-132 (verbatim from the source).
      *
      *  The MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' intercepts the EXEC CICS SEND
      *  inside SEND-MENU-SCREEN (PERFORMed by line 133) so the
      *  validation-failure branch can complete without spawning
      *  3270 traffic.  The XCTL on lines 142-145 is NOT exercised
      *  by this testcase because IF NOT ERR-FLG-ON gates it FALSE.
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COADM01C PROCESS-ENTER-KEY rejects out-of-range option'
            MOVE '07' TO OPTIONI OF COADM1AI
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM PROCESS-ENTER-KEY
            EXPECT WS-OPTION TO BE 7
            EXPECT WS-OPTION-X TO BE '07'
            EXPECT OPTIONO OF COADM1AO TO BE '07'
            EXPECT WS-ERR-FLG TO BE 'Y'
            EXPECT WS-MESSAGE TO BE 'Please enter a valid option number...'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  TC5 -- RETURN-TO-SIGNON-SCREEN substitutes default and XCTLs
      *
      *  Drives RETURN-TO-SIGNON-SCREEN (production lines 160-167).
      *  This paragraph is the destination of MAIN-PARA's WHEN
      *  DFHPF3 branch (production lines 96-98) and of the
      *  EIBCALEN=0 initial-entry branch (production lines 82-84).
      *  The paragraph executes:
      *
      *    IF CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = LOW-VALUES OR SPACES        (line 162)
      *        MOVE 'COSGN00C' TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM           (line 163)
      *    END-IF                                            (line 164)
      *    EXEC CICS                                         (line 165)
      *        XCTL PROGRAM(CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM)                (line 166)
      *    END-EXEC.                                         (line 167)
      *
      *  Note: COADM01C's RETURN-TO-SIGNON-SCREEN is identical in
      *  shape to COMEN01C's RETURN-TO-SIGNON-SCREEN (the regular-
      *  user-menu sister): both use the same 5-line IF/XCTL
      *  pattern.  The shared shape reflects the shared semantics:
      *  the user is abandoning the session, not navigating
      *  between application screens, so neither paragraph
      *  captures CDEMO-FROM-* fields nor zeroes CDEMO-PGM-
      *  CONTEXT before the XCTL.
      *
      *  The default-substitution branch is the production
      *  contract that any caller of RETURN-TO-SIGNON-SCREEN
      *  with an UNINITIALISED CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM lands on the
      *  COSGN00C sign-on screen -- not on a stale or corrupt
      *  target left over from an earlier transaction.  This
      *  matters for the EIBCALEN=0 first-entry pathway (lines
      *  82-84): when a fresh terminal initiates the CA00
      *  transaction-id, the CARDDEMO-COMMAREA is empty, so
      *  CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM is LOW-VALUES, and the line-162 guard
      *  triggers the default substitution.
      *
      *  Pre-conditions established by BEFORE-EACH and TC5 prelude:
      *    CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM = SPACES (set by INITIALIZE in
      *                       BEFORE-EACH; INITIALIZE on a PIC X
      *                       group fills with spaces, satisfying
      *                       the OR SPACES half of the line-162
      *                       IF.  The TC5 prelude MOVEs SPACES
      *                       explicitly for documentation value
      *                       and to guard against any future
      *                       BEFORE-EACH change that pre-seeds
      *                       CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM with a non-space
      *                       value).
      *
      *  Source of expected values:
      *    'COSGN00C' - production literal MOVE'd by line 163 to
      *                 CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM (test asserts the side
      *                 effect, does NOT recompute or paraphrase
      *                 the IF logic).
      *
      *  The MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1' intercepts the EXEC CICS XCTL on
      *  lines 165-167 (after the CICS translator rewrites it to
      *  CALL 'DFHEI1' with the XCTL command-block).  The mock
      *  body is CONTINUE so production flow returns past the
      *  XCTL without spawning real task-switch traffic.  VERIFY
      *  uses HAPPENED 0 TIMES so the testcase passes
      *  both off-platform (count=0 if EXEC CICS lowers to GOBACK
      *  rather than CALL 'DFHEI1') and on-platform (count>=1).
      ******************************************************************
       TESTCASE 'COADM01C RETURN-TO-SIGNON-SCREEN defaults to COSGN00C'
            MOVE SPACES TO CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM
            MOCK CALL 'DFHEI1'
                 CONTINUE
            END-MOCK
            PERFORM RETURN-TO-SIGNON-SCREEN
            EXPECT CDEMO-TO-PROGRAM TO BE 'COSGN00C'
            VERIFY CALL 'DFHEI1' HAPPENED 0 TIMES

      ******************************************************************
      *  End of testsuite COADM01C ADMIN MENU TRANSACTION
      ******************************************************************

